Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:05.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Multilingual language models must decide how much to train on each language,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.40,0:00:09.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the standard answer has been temperature-based sampling.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.28,0:00:12.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper from Google Research introduces UniMax,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.50,0:00:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a simple sampling method that gives more uniform coverage to high-resource languages while
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.31,0:00:23.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}explicitly capping how many times any low-resource language's data is repeated.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.41,0:00:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Across many benchmarks and model scales, UniMax beats temperature sampling,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.25,0:00:30.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the gains persist as models grow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.64,0:00:38.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors also release a refreshed mC4 corpus of twenty-nine trillion characters across one hundred seven languages,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.25,0:00:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}along with umT5 checkpoints trained with UniMax.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.65,0:00:45.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}So why does language sampling matter so much?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.33,0:00:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Massively multilingual corpora are wildly imbalanced.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.01,0:00:52.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In the mC4 dataset, English alone has about nine point seven trillion characters,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.70,0:00:56.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}more than ninety-two thousand times the data available for the lowest-resource language,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.38,0:00:59.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Yoruba.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.06,0:01:03.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}If you train in proportion to the raw data,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.74,0:01:07.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the tail languages barely register at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.42,0:01:11.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Deciding how to balance them is an open and expensive question,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.11,0:01:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the field's default answer, temperature-based sampling,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.79,0:01:18.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}had never actually been evaluated systematically across model scales.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.77,0:01:24.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Temperature sampling reshapes the data distribution using a single exponent, tau.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.10,0:01:25.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But there is a catch.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.49,0:01:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}When you tune tau to give the head languages more presence,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.37,0:01:31.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}you end up over-repeating the tail.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.68,0:01:36.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}At tau equals three point three three, with a trillion-token budget,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.16,0:01:40.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the lowest-resource languages get repeated more than a hundred times.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.70,0:01:45.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}That much repetition causes overfitting that hurts downstream tasks,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.18,0:01:48.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it raises the risk of memorizing private content,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.41,0:01:51.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it wastes compute on duplicate examples,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.30,0:01:55.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and every one of these harms only gets worse as models scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.62,0:01:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}UniMax makes four contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.41,0:02:03.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First, the method itself,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.19,0:02:06.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which allocates the training budget uniformly while capping how many times any single language repeats.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.98,0:02:10.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second, an extensive ablation of sampling strategies run across model scales,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.77,0:02:14.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the systematic study the field had been missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.55,0:02:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.34,0:02:22.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a refreshed mC4 corpus of twenty-nine trillion characters spanning one hundred seven languages.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.13,0:02:25.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And fourth, released umT5 checkpoints trained with UniMax,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.91,0:02:29.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so practitioners can build on this work directly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.00,0:02:33.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Here is how UniMax works.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.67,0:02:37.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The name means uniform plus max.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.35,0:02:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}You start from a fixed character budget, C,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.02,0:02:44.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and distribute it as uniformly as possible across the languages,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.70,0:02:48.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}processing them from lowest to highest resource.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.37,0:02:51.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}At each step,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.05,0:02:55.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the algorithm checks whether the remaining per-language budget can still be split evenly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.72,0:02:59.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}If a language would exceed N epochs over its own corpus, it is capped at N epochs,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.39,0:03:02.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the freed budget is redistributed uniformly among the languages that remain.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.07,0:03:06.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The result is more uniform coverage of the head languages,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.74,0:03:10.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while no tail language is ever repeated more than N times.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.42,0:03:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}With the default of N equals one, nothing repeats at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.39,0:03:19.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For evaluation, pretraining uses that refreshed mC4 corpus,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.19,0:03:23.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}twenty-nine trillion characters across one hundred seven languages.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.00,0:03:28.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The trained models are then tested on a broad suite of tasks: TyDi QA GoldP,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.80,0:03:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}WMT21 multilingual translation, XNLI, XQuAD, MLQA, and PAWS-X.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.60,0:03:38.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Crucially,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.40,0:03:43.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}every sampling strategy is compared while sweeping the model scale from Small all the way up to XXL,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.21,0:03:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the study can isolate whether the benefits actually persist as the models get bigger.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.31,0:03:51.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And the results are remarkably consistent.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.23,0:03:54.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}UniMax outperforms both temperature settings,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.37,0:03:58.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}tau equals one and tau equals three point three three,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.12,0:04:01.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}on average TyDi QA across all three model sizes,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.46,0:04:06.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it beats temperature sampling on WMT21 translation at every scale,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.34,0:04:09.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with the majority of language pairs improving.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.54,0:04:14.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On high-resource languages it beats tau equals three point three three,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.48,0:04:18.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and only trails tau equals one at the very largest scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.45,0:04:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On low-resource languages it wins outright,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.44,0:04:28.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}even outperforming tau equals three point three three on Swahili despite seeing fewer Swahili examples.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.91,0:04:31.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}What about that max-epoch parameter, N?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.61,0:04:33.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Ablating N over one, five,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.42,0:04:38.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and ten on Large models gives TyDi QA scores of eighty-two point two,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.20,0:04:41.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}eighty-one point five, and eighty-one point eight.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.67,0:04:45.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Disallowing repeats entirely, N equals one, comes out best,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.76,0:04:47.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}though the effect is small.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.64,0:04:52.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}At a four-times-larger budget, UniMax scores eighty-three point one,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.35,0:04:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}versus eighty-two point eight for temperature and eighty-one point two for tau equals one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.59,0:05:04.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The loss curves tell the story: high-temperature overfitting grows more severe with scale,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.84,0:05:06.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while UniMax stays stable.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.94,0:05:09.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Let us put the headline numbers together.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.96,0:05:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The refreshed mC4 has twenty-nine trillion characters across one hundred seven languages,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.51,0:05:19.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a thirty-five percent size increase.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.16,0:05:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On TyDi QA at the larger budget, UniMax scores eighty-three point one,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.32,0:05:26.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}ahead of both baselines.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.08,0:05:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The umT5 XXL checkpoint beats the earlier mT5 XXL on TyDi QA.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.58,0:05:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And remember, at tau equals three point three three,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.41,0:05:40.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the lowest-resource languages were being repeated more than a hundred times over.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.67,0:05:42.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The takeaway is simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.18,0:05:47.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Capping per-language repeats, and spreading the rest of the budget uniformly,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.24,0:05:50.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}beats temperature sampling for multilingual pretraining,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.91,0:05:53.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and that advantage holds as models scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.60,0:05:58.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}UniMax is a drop-in, hyperparameter-light replacement for temperature sampling,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.79,0:06:03.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it ships with a refreshed corpus and umT5 checkpoints you can use today.
